## TypeScript typing

### Naming conventions:

- Use PascalCase for all type and interface names.
- All hand-written enums must end with `Enum` (e.g. `UserRoleEnum`).
- All React component prop types must end with `Props` (e.g. `ButtonProps`).
- All function parameter types must end with `Params` (e.g. `CreateUserParams`).
